35,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
37,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
38,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
39,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
40,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh no, I found some really worrying news! Two of our outer wards lost their bus links, so it takes people an hour just to get to a counter. We really need to help them!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"That is quite distressing, @Yumi. Interestingly, my research shows that former outreach stops in those outer wards were remarkably popular, drawing more visitors than the main building does midweek. It seems the demand is certainly there.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The demand is irrelevant if we can't manage it. I've found that while we have some skilled volunteers, we have absolutely no one on the payroll trained to supervise outside facilitators. We are missing a critical layer of management.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Minako,,"I have found that our funding structure is precarious. County grants only cover session fees for the first year, meaning the operating budget must absorb those costs thereafter. Additionally, vehicle running costs overran significantly last year.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that our evening rooms are always full, but people are using the catalogue from home very late at night. Also, the scanning contractors have unreliable delivery windows.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, if the vehicle costs are already too high, does that mean a mobile service would be too expensive? But @Benjamin, if the outer wards really want the service, we have to find a way!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, it is a delicate balance. However, my findings also reveal that partner-run evening groups from six years ago still meet unaided. This suggests that community-led models are far more resilient than our own managed attempts.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, that's a convenient observation, but it proves my point. We lack the internal capacity to supervise. If we choose a service requiring professional certification or oversight, we're setting ourselves up for failure.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, you are correct that internal supervision is a risk. However, we must also consider that any service relying on the county grant will become a financial burden on our flat budget after one year. We need a model that is both manageable and fiscally sustainable.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about the scanning contractors. If their delivery windows keep slipping, a digital project might get delayed. But the late-night catalogue use shows people really want access when the building is closed.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that's so true! People are trying to use the library even when it's closed. But @Minako, if the bus links are gone, maybe we can't just rely on the building at all? We have to reach them!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, your passion is well-placed. Given that outreach was historically successful and community-led groups are enduring, we should prioritize a model that empowers the residents rather than one that relies on our own fragile infrastructure.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, empowering residents is a fine sentiment, but it's a gamble. If we lack the staff to supervise, we can't just hope for the best. We need a service that doesn't require specialized certification we can't maintain.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, I agree that we cannot gamble with safety or certification. However, we must also avoid a service that creates a permanent deficit in our operating budget. A model with low overhead and minimal staff supervision seems most logical.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we should be careful. If the rooms are full and the buses are gone, maybe something that doesn't require people to travel or wait for a building to open is best.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with @Daisuke! If people can't get here and the rooms are full, we need to be flexible. I really want to help those in the outer wards who are stranded!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are converging on a need for accessibility and sustainability. If we avoid high-maintenance infrastructure and instead leverage community resilience, we can serve those outer wards without risking a financial or managerial collapse.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, your ""community resilience"" is just a euphemism for lack of oversight. If we can't certify tools or supervise facilitators, we must avoid any proposal that requires technical certification or professional management. Logic dictates we choose the path of least risk.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I agree with @Shion that we must minimize risk. Given the budget's tendency to thin and the lack of supervisory staff, we should avoid high-overhead options like vehicles or specialized technical workshops. A low-maintenance, community-supported model is the most stable path.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we should look for something that doesn't depend on the buses or the building's hours. If we can reach people where they are, or online, it might be the safest way to help everyone.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
