65,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Looking at the options, I think Language Learning Circles are wonderful! They use partner organizations, which helps with the supervision @Shion mentioned, and they can happen across the district to help people without buses!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I find myself in agreement with @Yumi. The Language Learning Circles align perfectly with the success of the partner-run groups I discovered. It leverages community resilience while bypassing our internal supervisory deficits and the bus crisis.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, @Yumi, you've actually made a logical case. Since the circles are coordinated with partner organizations, the supervisory burden doesn't fall on our unqualified staff. It avoids the certification issues of the workshop and the costs of the mobile service.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree. The Language Learning Circles are the most sustainable choice. They avoid the high vehicle costs of the mobile service and the certification risks of the workshop, while the partner coordination protects our operating budget.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. The circles can happen across the district, so people without buses can still join. It seems like the best way to reach everyone without relying on the building's hours.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we all agree! It feels like the Language Learning Circles really solve all the problems we talked about. It's the kindest and most helpful choice for everyone in our community!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a rare pleasure when logic and empathy align so perfectly. By choosing a model that empowers partners, we avoid the pitfalls of our own administrative history and the current logistical failures.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Shion,,"It is the only option that doesn't create a new liability. We avoid the vehicle budget drain, the contractor delays, and the lack of certified staff. It is the most rational decision.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Indeed. It is the only proposal that addresses the accessibility issues without creating a long-term financial drain or a management crisis. It is a stable, scalable solution that fits our current constraints.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much better now that we've found a solution. It's a relief to know we can help the people in the outer wards without worrying about the buses or the building's limits. I'll vote for the circles.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'll definitely vote for the Language Learning Circles! It's just so wonderful that we found a way to bring people together and help everyone, no matter where they live!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,My vote is also for the Language Learning Circles. It is the only proposal that respects both the historical evidence of community success and our current institutional limitations.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Shion,,I will also vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is the only choice that logically bypasses our lack of supervisory staff and avoids unnecessary financial risk.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I will also vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is the most fiscally responsible and manageable option, ensuring we provide a service that remains viable long after the initial grant expires.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for the Language Learning Circles too. It's the best way to make sure everyone is included.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Yumi,,Yay! I'm so glad we could all work together to find the best answer. I'm voting for the Language Learning Circles!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
81,3,4,pass,Yumi,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
82,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"My vote is cast for the Language Learning Circles. It has been a most productive deliberation, and I am pleased that we have arrived at a conclusion based on evidence rather than mere intuition.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
